WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.216 --> 00:00:17.041
We made many improvements to our homes at Falconhurst and Tentholm.

2
00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:21.643
But there was one more improvement that my wife wanted us to make at Falconhurst.

3
00:00:22.524 --> 00:00:25.585
"I think that our nest in the tree is perfect," she said.

4
00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:29.887
"But I'd like to be able to reach it without climbing that dreadful ladder.

5
00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:32.148
Can you build a flight of steps?"

6
00:00:33.036 --> 00:00:36.939
"We might be able to build a staircase inside the trunk of the tree," I replied.

7
00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:39.981
"I've often suspected that the trunk is hollow.

8
00:00:40.622 --> 00:00:44.004
Didn't you say that you've noticed bees coming from a hole in the tree?"

9
00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:47.727
Before my wife could reply, little Franz piped up.

10
00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.088
"Oh yes!

11
00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:52.070
I went to look at them, and one stung me.

12
00:00:52.871 --> 00:00:55.253
I almost cried but I didn't."

13
00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:56.754
"Brave boy!"

14
00:00:56.974 --> 00:00:57.294
I said.

15
00:00:57.314 --> 00:00:59.236
"Let's see if the tree is really hollow."

16
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:03.945
Led by Jack, the boys were soon peeping into the hole.

17
00:01:04.705 --> 00:01:06.746
They tapped the tree to see if it sounded hollow.

18
00:01:07.587 --> 00:01:09.948
In their eagerness they forgot who lived in the tree.

19
00:01:10.748 --> 00:01:14.970
The bees, disturbed by all this activity, swarmed out and attacked the boys.

20
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.470
"Ow! Ow!

21
00:01:17.111 --> 00:01:18.171
Ow!" cried Jack.

22
00:01:18.191 --> 00:01:20.012
"Nasty bees!"

23
00:01:20.432 --> 00:01:22.353
said Fritz as he tried to swat them away.

24
00:01:23.213 --> 00:01:25.794
My wife and I pulled the boys away from the angry bees.

25
00:01:27.195 --> 00:01:29.456
They had all been stung on their hands and faces.

26
00:01:30.572 --> 00:01:35.536
Before we built a staircase, we removed the bees to a new nesting place in a large gourd.

27
00:01:36.277 --> 00:01:39.700
We made good use of the honey and wax that they left behind in the tree.

28
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.162
Then we began working on the stairs.

29
00:01:43.143 --> 00:01:46.025
At the base of the tree, we made an opening for a door.

30
00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:50.108
We attached a door we'd taken earlier from the captain's cabin.

31
00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:55.113
Next we cleared out the rotted wood from the center of the trunk and put up a stout

32
00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:57.034
sapling to provide a center pole.

33
00:01:57.795 --> 00:02:00.481
With planks from the wreck, we then fashioned steps.

34
00:02:01.542 --> 00:02:04.644
As we worked, we cut windows in the trunk for light and air.

35
00:02:05.504 --> 00:02:09.807
When we reached the top of the center pole, we added another sapling to reach the floor of

36
00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:10.688
our home above.

37
00:02:11.368 --> 00:02:13.110
We even included two handrails!

38
00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:19.254
This task took us a whole month, during which we also had to care for our animals.

39
00:02:20.154 --> 00:02:23.157
By now several of the goats and sheep had produced offspring.

40
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.820
To keep these frisky youngsters from straying, we tied bells around their necks.

41
00:02:28.908 --> 00:02:30.909
Juno produced a fine litter of puppies.

42
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:38.073
Jack introduced his little jackal, Fangs, to the litter, and, to his delight, Juno adopted the wild dog.

43
00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:41.775
The other pets were also flourishing and learning new tasks.

44
00:02:42.656 --> 00:02:48.899
After giving us much trouble, Storm, the buffalo, was now capable of carrying both people and things.

45
00:02:49.779 --> 00:02:55.342
Fritz was so busy teaching his eagle, Pounce, to hunt live prey that he gave Knips to Ernest.

46
00:02:56.143 --> 00:03:00.850
Knips was not allowed to remain idle, as Ernest decided that he should be taught to do something

47
00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.033
useful. He and Jack made a small basket that fit on the monkey's back.

48
00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:10.637
Then Ernest taught Knips to climb coconut and other tall trees and to bring down the fruit in

49
00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:11.178
the basket.

50
00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:18.003
Jack tried to teach Fangs to retrieve, but the jackal kept eating everything it caught.

51
00:03:19.844 --> 00:03:24.288
Meanwhile I was determined to have some waterproof boots before the start of the rainy season.

52
00:03:25.024 --> 00:03:29.285
To make a mold, I filled a pair of socks with sand and coated them with a thin

53
00:03:29.325 --> 00:03:30.065
layer of clay.

54
00:03:30.886 --> 00:03:32.886
Then I brushed on several layers of rubber.

55
00:03:33.566 --> 00:03:37.927
When that had dried, I broke the mold and added some buffalo-hide soles.

56
00:03:37.947 --> 00:03:40.248
"These are wonderful!"

57
00:03:40.588 --> 00:03:42.229
said Fritz as he tried on my boots.

58
00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:44.089
"Can you make me a pair?"

59
00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:45.870
"Me too!"

60
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.410
cried all the other boys.

61
00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:53.171
I was delighted to fill their orders, and soon everyone in the family had a pair of comfortable,

62
00:03:53.352 --> 00:03:54.732
durable waterproof boots.

63
00:03:55.636 --> 00:04:00.018
The boys had long been complaining about having to walk to the stream and bring back heavy buckets

64
00:04:00.059 --> 00:04:00.479
of water.

65
00:04:01.199 --> 00:04:05.061
So our next job was to build a dam with a series of pipes to carry the water

66
00:04:05.101 --> 00:04:05.822
to Falconhurst.

67
00:04:07.022 --> 00:04:12.245
One day, as we were finishing this task, we were startled by the roaring or bellowing of a

68
00:04:12.325 --> 00:04:13.066
wild beast.

69
00:04:14.106 --> 00:04:17.548
The sound was so strange that I couldn't imagine what animal had made it.

70
00:04:17.568 --> 00:04:20.189
"Perhaps it's a lion," offered Jack.

71
00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:22.691
"No, a gorilla," said Fritz.

72
00:04:22.711 --> 00:04:25.625
"More likely a hyena," said Ernest.

73
00:04:25.645 --> 00:04:29.889
"Whatever it is," I said, "we must be ready when it arrives.

74
00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:33.572
All of you, hurry to the nest while I secure the door."

75
00:04:34.613 --> 00:04:39.097
I left the dogs outside to protect our animals, closed the door, and joined my family.

76
00:04:39.898 --> 00:04:41.199
Every eye was on watch.

77
00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.501
Every gun was loaded.

78
00:04:44.402 --> 00:04:46.084
The dreadful sound came nearer.
